<title>FRANCE: Credit Agricole 96 net attrib up 15 pct.</title>
<headline>Credit Agricole 96 net attrib up 15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in billions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			     7.5  vs	     6.5</p>
<p>    Gross operating profit		    26.4  vs	    24.5</p>
<p>    Net banking income			  73.8  vs	    66</p>
<p>    Provisions				    12.0  vs	    12.4</p>
<p>    Client credits			   1,205    vs	 1,015</p>
<p>    Client deposits			  1,345    vs	 1,137</p>
<p>    Cooke Ratio (%)			     10.4  vs	    10.5</p>
<p>-----------</p>
<p>Banque Indosuez</p>
<p>    Net attributable profit (million)    362    vs	   107</p>
<p>    Net banking income			  12.5	 (up 15 pct)</p>
<p>    Provisions				     2.0  vs   (not given)</p>
<p>    Gross operating				3.5	 (up 64 pct)</p>
<p>NOTE - Giving its results in a statement, Credit Agricole said that given the timing of its purchase of Indosuez -- 51 percent by July 1, 1996, and 100 percent by December 23 -- the accounts integrated 100 percent of the Indosuez balance sheet but only the results for the second half.</p>
<p>On constant structure basis, net banking income would have been 67 billion francs, up 1.5 percent.</p>
</text>
